(357594, 28812, 5475, '<td valign="top">What a great shot!  I thought of doing something like this, but chose another subject instead.  I''m glad, because my idea would not have stood a chance against your wonderful shot!  I like the background image being blurred, and that it is in BW.  Color in the background would have competed for attention with the rings.   Actually, I do see a small amount of color in the bride''s arm and at the left in the frame.  I won''t mark down the score for that, no sense in penalizing you for following the rules.  The only constructive criticism I can think of is the composition.  I like the rule of thirds, and I would like it if the rings were not centered vertically.  That is a minor point, though, and I predict a high score for your shot this week.  Great job!<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'What a great shot!  I thought of doing something like this, but chose another subject instead.  I''m glad, because my idea would not have stood a chance against your wonderful shot!  I like the background image being blurred, and that it is in BW.  Color in the background would have competed for attention with the rings.   Actually, I do see a small amount of color in the bride''s arm and at the left in the frame.  I won''t mark down the score for that, no sense in penalizing you for following the rules.  The only constructive criticism I can think of is the composition.  I like the rule of thirds, and I would like it if the rings were not centered vertically.  That is a minor point, though, and I predict a high score for your shot this week.  Great job!JD Anderson', '2003-07-16 01:51:28.000000', NULL, 1),
