(357606, 28453, 5475, '<td valign="top">This is so cool!  I like industrial shots, but the patina, or old paint, whatever it is really gives this shot some impact.  composition is great, as is focus, lighting, DOF.  If this were my image, I would try to bump up the contrast a little, either with a contrast adjustment, or a curves adjustment.  Another way to increase contrast (not DPC legal, though) in Photoshop is to creat a new layer on top, go to layer&gt;new fill layer&gt; solid color.  Change the mode to color burn, then hit OK.  A color picker will pop up, select a light gray color and hit OK.  Works great!<br/>Congrats on a very nice image and good luck.<br/>JD Anderson</td>', 'This is so cool!  I like industrial shots, but the patina, or old paint, whatever it is really gives this shot some impact.  composition is great, as is focus, lighting, DOF.  If this were my image, I would try to bump up the contrast a little, either with a contrast adjustment, or a curves adjustment.  Another way to increase contrast (not DPC legal, though) in Photoshop is to creat a new layer on top, go to layer>new fill layer> solid color.  Change the mode to color burn, then hit OK.  A color picker will pop up, select a light gray color and hit OK.  Works great!Congrats on a very nice image and good luck.JD Anderson', '2003-07-16 01:55:57.000000', NULL, 1),
