(360101, 28940, 1005, '<td valign="top">I, too, did a shot of the moon.  I''m sorry, but the clarity isn''t very strong and the colored grain detracts from the image heavily.  4 Rob the Swash</td>', 'I, too, did a shot of the moon.  I''m sorry, but the clarity isn''t very strong and the colored grain detracts from the image heavily.  4 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-17 19:47:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(360103, 28184, 1005, '<td valign="top">I too did a shot of the moon for this challenge.  I''m sorry, but the clarity isn''t very strong.  Two suggestions - if you''re in a heavily populated area, try going out in the boonies more (less smog interferance) and second, if you have a tripod, use it.  4 Rob the Swash</td>', 'I too did a shot of the moon for this challenge.  I''m sorry, but the clarity isn''t very strong.  Two suggestions - if you''re in a heavily populated area, try going out in the boonies more (less smog interferance) and second, if you have a tripod, use it.  4 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-17 19:49:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(360104, 28773, 1005, '<td valign="top">Nice view of a very full moon (You must have taken this on the last day of the challenge).  I, too, did a moon shot (the day before yours, not as full).  You have a decent amount of detail, but the upper part of the moon isn''t very sharp.  I started you as a 5, but upgrading to a 6...Rob the Swash</td>', 'Nice view of a very full moon (You must have taken this on the last day of the challenge).  I, too, did a moon shot (the day before yours, not as full).  You have a decent amount of detail, but the upper part of the moon isn''t very sharp.  I started you as a 5, but upgrading to a 6...Rob the Swash', '2003-07-17 19:52:04.000000', NULL, 1),
(360106, 28886, 1005, '<td valign="top">I like the clouds, it creates a neat effect, but it seems like the camera tried to focus on those clouds as the moon isn''t as sharp.  Must have been the last day of the challenge (I did mine the day before and the moon wasn''t quite full).  5 Rob the Swash</td>', 'I like the clouds, it creates a neat effect, but it seems like the camera tried to focus on those clouds as the moon isn''t as sharp.  Must have been the last day of the challenge (I did mine the day before and the moon wasn''t quite full).  5 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-17 19:53:36.000000', NULL, 1),
