(360923, 28421, 1005, '<td valign="top">Good focus...is your lighting a flashlight? (Seems a bit too strong in places)  Good thing I don''t score titles as I really don''t understand this one.  Challenge met.  I nearly missed the contact lens, barely visible.  6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Good focus...is your lighting a flashlight? (Seems a bit too strong in places)  Good thing I don''t score titles as I really don''t understand this one.  Challenge met.  I nearly missed the contact lens, barely visible.  6 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 19:36:12.000000', NULL, 1),
(360926, 28289, 1005, '<td valign="top">Cute dog shot.  Photo-wise, I''m not too keen on this shot.  I think this was a spur of the moment type shot (looks like it), but the dog looks like a co-operative one (meaning you might have been able to capture the spirit of this shot, with a more careful set up and the dog probably would have worked with you).  The background is too busy and the lighting not strong enough on the subject.   6 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Cute dog shot.  Photo-wise, I''m not too keen on this shot.  I think this was a spur of the moment type shot (looks like it), but the dog looks like a co-operative one (meaning you might have been able to capture the spirit of this shot, with a more careful set up and the dog probably would have worked with you).  The background is too busy and the lighting not strong enough on the subject.   6 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 19:40:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(360927, 28645, 715, '<td valign="top">Wow, what a great shot!</td>', 'Wow, what a great shot!', '2003-07-18 19:40:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(360934, 28911, 4049, '<td valign="top">lol</td>', 'lol', '2003-07-18 19:48:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(360936, 28410, 4049, '<td valign="top">pretty</td>', 'pretty', '2003-07-18 19:51:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(360941, 29093, 715, '<td valign="top">Very good approach of the challenge and very well composed. Just too bad that the brightness of the wall behind the boy  is too overwhelming. Despite that, good job!<br/></td>', 'Very good approach of the challenge and very well composed. Just too bad that the brightness of the wall behind the boy  is too overwhelming. Despite that, good job!', '2003-07-18 19:54:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(360943, 28939, 6172, '<td valign="top">Very interesting.  I would like to know how this was done.  Lots of "Round"!  Maybe it''s my monitor, but it looks a little grey to me, like it could use more contrast.</td>', 'Very interesting.  I would like to know how this was done.  Lots of "Round"!  Maybe it''s my monitor, but it looks a little grey to me, like it could use more contrast.', '2003-07-18 20:00:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(360946, 28228, 6172, '<td valign="top">Yes, but it''s all too obvious how.  Nice photo.</td>', 'Yes, but it''s all too obvious how.  Nice photo.', '2003-07-18 20:02:08.000000', NULL, 1),
(360947, 29109, 9337, '<td valign="top">This is a neat image, I''ve never really seen anything quite like this before. There doesn''t appear to be any particular object in focus. Nothing''s jumping out at me.</td>', 'This is a neat image, I''ve never really seen anything quite like this before. There doesn''t appear to be any particular object in focus. Nothing''s jumping out at me.', '2003-07-18 20:02:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(360951, 29119, 2158, '<td valign="top">I don''t mind the out of focus marbles at the back (top) of the picture, but I find the front ones rather distracting.</td>', 'I don''t mind the out of focus marbles at the back (top) of the picture, but I find the front ones rather distracting.', '2003-07-18 20:09:10.000000', NULL, 1),
(360952, 29132, 1005, '<td valign="top">Neat shot!  I like the clouds reflected in the marble, nice touch.  Nit time - (no score effect, true nits)  - dust on your lens or glass; not enough blue in the marble (for good balance); and some extra stray white ghosts in front of the flag (I think it''s more reflections, but not certain).  I consider all of these to be minor flaws, but the idea is very good and for the most part well executed.  9 Rob the Swash<br/>(Interesting shot and a nice variation from the water droplets theme that had been so heavily done here)</td>', 'Neat shot!  I like the clouds reflected in the marble, nice touch.  Nit time - (no score effect, true nits)  - dust on your lens or glass; not enough blue in the marble (for good balance); and some extra stray white ghosts in front of the flag (I think it''s more reflections, but not certain).  I consider all of these to be minor flaws, but the idea is very good and for the most part well executed.  9 Rob the Swash(Interesting shot and a nice variation from the water droplets theme that had been so heavily done here)', '2003-07-18 20:09:16.000000', NULL, 1),
(360953, 28376, 9337, '<td valign="top">I remember those days VERY exciting. The perspective is very interesting and I''m assuming the softness is intentional, it feels a little too soft.</td>', 'I remember those days VERY exciting. The perspective is very interesting and I''m assuming the softness is intentional, it feels a little too soft.', '2003-07-18 20:09:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(360954, 28208, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very cool!  The eye is perfect, I love it!  The feathers range from very good and nicely textured, to well less than that.  A bit of grain on the beak, but not as bad as some of my shots.  The eye is a real "eye catcher"!  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very cool!  The eye is perfect, I love it!  The feathers range from very good and nicely textured, to well less than that.  A bit of grain on the beak, but not as bad as some of my shots.  The eye is a real "eye catcher"!  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:11:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(360955, 28420, 9337, '<td valign="top">This image feels a little too grainy and grey for my liking. I see the round apples(I think they''re apples) in the tree above but I don''t feel like it''s a main theme of the picture. Great job not blowing the highlights shooting into the sun.</td>', 'This image feels a little too grainy and grey for my liking. I see the round apples(I think they''re apples) in the tree above but I don''t feel like it''s a main theme of the picture. Great job not blowing the highlights shooting into the sun.', '2003-07-18 20:11:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(360957, 28812, 9337, '<td valign="top">I very much like this photo. I started shooting my own wedding band, but I just couldn''t find a perspective I liked. The DOF here is great, accentuates the theme. How did you get that angle on the background with the rings flat?</td>', 'I very much like this photo. I started shooting my own wedding band, but I just couldn''t find a perspective I liked. The DOF here is great, accentuates the theme. How did you get that angle on the background with the rings flat?', '2003-07-18 20:12:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(360959, 28419, 9337, '<td valign="top">Interesting concept. I haven''t seen any euro''s yet so it''s neet to see some. The coins look very flat against that background. I''m not sure if changing the lighting would help as I''m still learning.</td>', 'Interesting concept. I haven''t seen any euro''s yet so it''s neet to see some. The coins look very flat against that background. I''m not sure if changing the lighting would help as I''m still learning.', '2003-07-18 20:14:23.000000', NULL, 1),
(360960, 29031, 1005, '<td valign="top">That''s a beauty!  Looks like a variation of the Morphius family.  (I have a blue morphious, from the Macro challenge).  I like everything about this photo, except for the left crop, the right side is very close to chopping an antennea, but the left definately chops it''s rear.  Very nice color!  Good focus (it helps when the b-fly is "flat" to the camera).  Where was this butterfly exhibit located?  (I locate and go to as many as I can find!!!)  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'That''s a beauty!  Looks like a variation of the Morphius family.  (I have a blue morphious, from the Macro challenge).  I like everything about this photo, except for the left crop, the right side is very close to chopping an antennea, but the left definately chops it''s rear.  Very nice color!  Good focus (it helps when the b-fly is "flat" to the camera).  Where was this butterfly exhibit located?  (I locate and go to as many as I can find!!!)  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:15:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(360963, 29179, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice contrast between the round bails in white and the flat-topped, red mesa.  Focus seems very good.  I would have upped the color saturation, but then again, I like VERY strong colors.  (This is probably more true to life...)  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice contrast between the round bails in white and the flat-topped, red mesa.  Focus seems very good.  I would have upped the color saturation, but then again, I like VERY strong colors.  (This is probably more true to life...)  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:16:45.000000', NULL, 1),
(360964, 28063, 9337, '<td valign="top">Interesting perspective on the cat. It doesn''t jump out at me, I wonder if that would change seeing more of its head. I thought red eye on cats was green, interesting affect.</td>', 'Interesting perspective on the cat. It doesn''t jump out at me, I wonder if that would change seeing more of its head. I thought red eye on cats was green, interesting affect.', '2003-07-18 20:16:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(360965, 28988, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very pretty and nice rich colors.  If anything, it might be a little too centered, but then again, I''m not a total fan of the rule of thirds, so nice shot!  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very pretty and nice rich colors.  If anything, it might be a little too centered, but then again, I''m not a total fan of the rule of thirds, so nice shot!  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:18:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(360967, 28455, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very, very cool!  It does look like something you''d see in space.  Very interesting shot, great color..I''d like to play with one of these things...looks like fun!  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very, very cool!  It does look like something you''d see in space.  Very interesting shot, great color..I''d like to play with one of these things...looks like fun!  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:20:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(360968, 29114, 4049, '<td valign="top">too dark</td>', 'too dark', '2003-07-18 20:22:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(360969, 28465, 9337, '<td valign="top">Interesting shot, I wonder what they''re looking at. I wish I could see a little more of the iris. Was that detail lost in the greyscale conversion?</td>', 'Interesting shot, I wonder what they''re looking at. I wish I could see a little more of the iris. Was that detail lost in the greyscale conversion?', '2003-07-18 20:22:52.000000', NULL, 1),
(360970, 28706, 1005, '<td valign="top">Very nice!  Sepia seems very correct for this one.  I like the water splashes.  The sepia seems a good choice for the sky background, too.  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Very nice!  Sepia seems very correct for this one.  I like the water splashes.  The sepia seems a good choice for the sky background, too.  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:24:21.000000', NULL, 1),
(360974, 28110, 1005, '<td valign="top">Did the dog bite the bubble?  I love the colors and reflection in the bubble, VERY nice!  But it seems a little pixelated at the bottom...I wonder why?  The rest is so very clear!  9 Rob the Swash</td>', 'Did the dog bite the bubble?  I love the colors and reflection in the bubble, VERY nice!  But it seems a little pixelated at the bottom...I wonder why?  The rest is so very clear!  9 Rob the Swash', '2003-07-18 20:26:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(360978, 28426, 9337, '<td valign="top">Ahh the globe. Sure is a round world. Grey scale is neat, lighting is dramatic. For some reason the content doesn''t excite me.</td>', 'Ahh the globe. Sure is a round world. Grey scale is neat, lighting is dramatic. For some reason the content doesn''t excite me.', '2003-07-18 20:31:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(360979, 28410, 7969, '<td valign="top">Your photo, IMO is very overprocessed, yet a great example of a pushed photo that works.  It has taken on almost a water color feel to it.  My only dislike is the top I find it distracting and would of prefered it cropped out. Otherwise i quite like your shot the flower buds on the left  and the vast space on right is very nice.  Good work.</td>', 'Your photo, IMO is very overprocessed, yet a great example of a pushed photo that works.  It has taken on almost a water color feel to it.  My only dislike is the top I find it distracting and would of prefered it cropped out. Otherwise i quite like your shot the flower buds on the left  and the vast space on right is very nice.  Good work.', '2003-07-18 20:31:16.000000', NULL, 1);
INSERT INTO comments ("id", "image_id", "commenter_id", "raw_comment", "comment", "date", "edited", "made_during_challenge") VALUES
(360980, 28775, 9337, '<td valign="top">Neat effect, I like the colors. The photo seems grainy on my computer.</td>', 'Neat effect, I like the colors. The photo seems grainy on my computer.', '2003-07-18 20:36:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(360981, 29157, 7969, '<td valign="top">What a fun and funny shot.  I like that all of their expressions are very similar, yet each different.  I am sure this is a photo they will love you to show boyfriends in a few years :  ).</td>', 'What a fun and funny shot.  I like that all of their expressions are very similar, yet each different.  I am sure this is a photo they will love you to show boyfriends in a few years :  ).', '2003-07-18 20:36:47.000000', NULL, 1),
