(364287, 29016, 9073, '<td valign="top">*critique club*<br/> <br/>Overall<br/>You''ve set out to meet the challenge by presenting a photograph which contains many circles. You meet the challenge directly.<br/> <br/>Composition<br/>This photograph is designed according to the rule of thirds. The main line of circles falls exactly on the upper third line and the circle in the bottom right on the right third line. The top left background is blue and the bottom right, green. Primary colours balancing each other. <br/> <br/>Colours<br/>I''m not sure about the exposure here. Old machinery should have a rust colour, or, if polished, should be bright. The off-brown colour range here doesn''t seem to fit my knowledge of machine colours. The silver areas are a little weak, and if brighter, would have helped the colour range.<br/> <br/>Concept<br/>There''s a true sense of irony here. Roundness usually has the feeling of pleasantness, warmth, comfort. You''ve chosen to counterplay this with an instrument of destruction, of war. By chosing a camera position very close to the machine, you take us right into the detail of war. This is a very unpleasant image, I feel. The primary background is also well-chosen. The blue is man-made, the green, natural. This strengthens the sense that war is both man-made and natural. Scary. <br/> <br/>Conclusion<br/>I would have liked for the colours to have been more accurate, or more vivid, depending on how you choose to portray your meaning. The crop, the camera angle, the dof are all good. <br/> <br/>Best wishes<br/> <br/>Jim</td>', '*critique club* OverallYou''ve set out to meet the challenge by presenting a photograph which contains many circles. You meet the challenge directly. CompositionThis photograph is designed according to the rule of thirds. The main line of circles falls exactly on the upper third line and the circle in the bottom right on the right third line. The top left background is blue and the bottom right, green. Primary colours balancing each other.  ColoursI''m not sure about the exposure here. Old machinery should have a rust colour, or, if polished, should be bright. The off-brown colour range here doesn''t seem to fit my knowledge of machine colours. The silver areas are a little weak, and if brighter, would have helped the colour range. ConceptThere''s a true sense of irony here. Roundness usually has the feeling of pleasantness, warmth, comfort. You''ve chosen to counterplay this with an instrument of destruction, of war. By chosing a camera position very close to the machine, you take us right into the detail of war. This is a very unpleasant image, I feel. The primary background is also well-chosen. The blue is man-made, the green, natural. This strengthens the sense that war is both man-made and natural. Scary.  ConclusionI would have liked for the colours to have been more accurate, or more vivid, depending on how you choose to portray your meaning. The crop, the camera angle, the dof are all good.  Best wishes Jim', '2003-07-23 03:45:08.000000', NULL, 0),
(364289, 29019, 9932, '<td valign="top">Willem<br/> <br/>Excellent! Congratulations. It was so hard to find anything wrong with a photograph of this quality. Well thought out and very well edited. I only hope someday I can produce a photo of the same quality.<br/> <br/>Calvus<br/> <br/></td>', 'Willem Excellent! Congratulations. It was so hard to find anything wrong with a photograph of this quality. Well thought out and very well edited. I only hope someday I can produce a photo of the same quality. Calvus ', '2003-07-23 03:48:43.000000', NULL, 0),
(364304, 28325, 10110, '<td valign="top">Well, this did alot better than i thought! It was a last minute idea, it''s a clock that was made for my dad''s birthday by one of his friends and was taken with it still on the wall and with full flash (hence the harsh lighting and shadows that were mentioned). <br/>I thought this fit the challenge title ''round'' quite well, as it was both a clock and a record. I think if it was just a picture of a record as suggested it would''ve had less character and scored far less.<br/>Thankyou to everyone who voted, and i''m very grateful for the comments that were left.</td>', 'Well, this did alot better than i thought! It was a last minute idea, it''s a clock that was made for my dad''s birthday by one of his friends and was taken with it still on the wall and with full flash (hence the harsh lighting and shadows that were mentioned). I thought this fit the challenge title ''round'' quite well, as it was both a clock and a record. I think if it was just a picture of a record as suggested it would''ve had less character and scored far less.Thankyou to everyone who voted, and i''m very grateful for the comments that were left.', '2003-07-23 03:58:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(364383, 28576, 7857, '<td valign="top">Hmmmm... I didn''t think of this at the time but this is more of a UK only thing. These are conkers and come from the horse chestnut tree, when they are ready they open up and the large brown seed (conker) inside is collected by school kids to use in a school yard game. It was only after I got a couple of the comments that I realised that few people would actually know what they were!<br/> <br/>Never mind, bring on the next challenge.</td>', 'Hmmmm... I didn''t think of this at the time but this is more of a UK only thing. These are conkers and come from the horse chestnut tree, when they are ready they open up and the large brown seed (conker) inside is collected by school kids to use in a school yard game. It was only after I got a couple of the comments that I realised that few people would actually know what they were! Never mind, bring on the next challenge.', '2003-07-23 04:41:30.000000', NULL, 0),
