(365002, 28865, 6999, '<td valign="top">Matt - your critique club moment is at hand. damn I''m glad to see this one come up, after our convversation about that other shot of yours.<br/> <br/>My first reaction is surprise that it only placed 7th, but it does step on the toes of the ''literal representation of others works of art'' rule quite heavily. <br/> <br/>What I love about this, and what for me perhaps puts it above all the other shots I''ve seen in the challenge, is the light: not only is it the perfect light to shape this image, and to give a real sense of three dimensions to the do-nut, but you''ve also caught the colour ttemperatre of it perfectly: the warmness of it on the wall to the left of frame is marvellous.<br/> <br/>The circular border effect (however it''s achieved) works perfectly too. My first impression of this, on seeing the thumbnail, was that  it was an eye - and that feeling still hasn''t quite gone away after looking at it for quite a while.<br/> <br/>I''m not goig to begin to criticise this technically - there''s quite obviously nothing wrong with it: it''s the first shot i''ve added to my favourites in quite a little while. Must be getting picky in my old age.<br/> <br/>Congratulations on a fine photo.<br/> <br/>ed</td>', 'Matt - your critique club moment is at hand. damn I''m glad to see this one come up, after our convversation about that other shot of yours. My first reaction is surprise that it only placed 7th, but it does step on the toes of the ''literal representation of others works of art'' rule quite heavily.  What I love about this, and what for me perhaps puts it above all the other shots I''ve seen in the challenge, is the light: not only is it the perfect light to shape this image, and to give a real sense of three dimensions to the do-nut, but you''ve also caught the colour ttemperatre of it perfectly: the warmness of it on the wall to the left of frame is marvellous. The circular border effect (however it''s achieved) works perfectly too. My first impression of this, on seeing the thumbnail, was that  it was an eye - and that feeling still hasn''t quite gone away after looking at it for quite a while. I''m not goig to begin to criticise this technically - there''s quite obviously nothing wrong with it: it''s the first shot i''ve added to my favourites in quite a little while. Must be getting picky in my old age. Congratulations on a fine photo. ed', '2003-07-23 14:19:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(365013, 28934, 10219, '<td valign="top">I really expected to do better with this photo than what I did.  If you have any more suggestions, please let me know!</td>', 'I really expected to do better with this photo than what I did.  If you have any more suggestions, please let me know!', '2003-07-23 14:30:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(365016, 28410, 9977, '<td valign="top">Thank You all for your very constructive comments, I am quite new in digital photography and digital pictures manipulations(I swapped a old 28-70 2.8L Canon for a Leica digilux), I am very happy but it is a different way to manage pictures... I tried not to change too much things in the original picture (it''s why it''s not cropped), and with Photoshop Elements I only done an auto levels correction, and that''s all (or maybe I tried a sharpening) I was not very happy with the shot quality but all your comments will help me to enhance and learn to manage digital imagery... Thank you all ...<br/>I am looking for a Canon Eos 10D for around 900-1000$, someone interested selling me one ??<br/>(I have still canon analog EOS3 body and 2 Canon L Zoom lenses, and would like to use them ... in digital)...<br/> <br/>Thank you all<br/>Rui Felipe</td>', 'Thank You all for your very constructive comments, I am quite new in digital photography and digital pictures manipulations(I swapped a old 28-70 2.8L Canon for a Leica digilux), I am very happy but it is a different way to manage pictures... I tried not to change too much things in the original picture (it''s why it''s not cropped), and with Photoshop Elements I only done an auto levels correction, and that''s all (or maybe I tried a sharpening) I was not very happy with the shot quality but all your comments will help me to enhance and learn to manage digital imagery... Thank you all ...I am looking for a Canon Eos 10D for around 900-1000$, someone interested selling me one ??(I have still canon analog EOS3 body and 2 Canon L Zoom lenses, and would like to use them ... in digital)... Thank you allRui Felipe', '2003-07-23 14:37:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(365053, 29184, 715, '<td valign="top">I''m very surprised too. Congrats with a great photo though. I added it to my list of favorites.</td>', 'I''m very surprised too. Congrats with a great photo though. I added it to my list of favorites.', '2003-07-23 15:10:56.000000', NULL, 0),
(365067, 28410, 9977, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ellamay:</b></div><hr/><i>Your photo, IMO is very overprocessed, yet a great example of a pushed photo that works.  It has taken on almost a water color feel to it.  My only dislike is the top I find it distracting and would of prefered it cropped out. Otherwise i quite like your shot the flower buds on the left  and the vast space on right is very nice.  Good work.</i></td></tr></table> <br/>I think I don''t merit this place, anyway I am very motivated to follow your comments, it''s very kind of you ...<br/>I don''t pushed the picture, I done just an autolevel in Photoshop elements (it''s new for me, i used to work in a little B&amp;W darkroom not in front of my computer ...) and I was not really happy with my composition, but I red the rules, and kept that we could''nt not change too much things on the original picture, and I was afraid of changing forbidden things (I don''t yet understand all that technical stuff ...)..<br/>Hope you can help me as I can help you ... Thank you again <br/></td>', 'Originally posted by ellamay:Your photo, IMO is very overprocessed, yet a great example of a pushed photo that works.  It has taken on almost a water color feel to it.  My only dislike is the top I find it distracting and would of prefered it cropped out. Otherwise i quite like your shot the flower buds on the left  and the vast space on right is very nice.  Good work. I think I don''t merit this place, anyway I am very motivated to follow your comments, it''s very kind of you ...I don''t pushed the picture, I done just an autolevel in Photoshop elements (it''s new for me, i used to work in a little B&W darkroom not in front of my computer ...) and I was not really happy with my composition, but I red the rules, and kept that we could''nt not change too much things on the original picture, and I was afraid of changing forbidden things (I don''t yet understand all that technical stuff ...)..Hope you can help me as I can help you ... Thank you again ', '2003-07-23 15:20:54.000000', NULL, 0),
(365078, 28985, 1005, '<td valign="top">Naturally set shots like this don''t do well at DPC.  It requires a bit of thought and doesn''t contain a lot of WOW.  I like this and scored it an 8.  I would bet money this was "carved" out, unless there was a cliff and an old stream bed right there.  Compositionally, this is fine.  I might have tried a steeper angle, or moved around to catch different reflections in the water.  Splashing the water might have created some fun effects, but I can''t think of a way without putting stones into the pond...probably not a good idea.  Rob</td>', 'Naturally set shots like this don''t do well at DPC.  It requires a bit of thought and doesn''t contain a lot of WOW.  I like this and scored it an 8.  I would bet money this was "carved" out, unless there was a cliff and an old stream bed right there.  Compositionally, this is fine.  I might have tried a steeper angle, or moved around to catch different reflections in the water.  Splashing the water might have created some fun effects, but I can''t think of a way without putting stones into the pond...probably not a good idea.  Rob', '2003-07-23 15:37:50.000000', NULL, 0),
(365107, 29096, 2152, '<td valign="top">*shakes head*<br/> <br/>It''s a shame so many people could not appreciate this.  Don''t take the score personally, it''s just that the majority here don''t see the merits of photographs that are anything other than tack sharp.  The great comments you received should offer some consolation...</td>', '*shakes head* It''s a shame so many people could not appreciate this.  Don''t take the score personally, it''s just that the majority here don''t see the merits of photographs that are anything other than tack sharp.  The great comments you received should offer some consolation...', '2003-07-23 16:19:03.000000', NULL, 0),
