(365900, 28760, 9972, '<td valign="top">THE BEST SHOT WITH MARBLES IVE SEEN. I LIKE THE PERSPECTIVE ON THIS. LOOKS LIKE ITS ABOUT TO ROLL ELEGANTLY OFF SOMEWHERE. I NOTICED YOU THOUGHT YOU GOT ROBBED.....IN MY BOOKS... YEAH AT LEAST A LITTLE.<br/>EXCELLENT WORK.</td>', 'THE BEST SHOT WITH MARBLES IVE SEEN. I LIKE THE PERSPECTIVE ON THIS. LOOKS LIKE ITS ABOUT TO ROLL ELEGANTLY OFF SOMEWHERE. I NOTICED YOU THOUGHT YOU GOT ROBBED.....IN MY BOOKS... YEAH AT LEAST A LITTLE.EXCELLENT WORK.', '2003-07-24 09:56:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(365921, 29129, 9972, '<td valign="top">I DONT SEE A LOT OF ROUND. I DONT FEEL ROUND. WILL SCORE POORLY FOR THOSE FACTS (DID IN FACT). HOWEVER I LIKE IT FOR ABSTRACTNESS. THE COLORS ARE COOL. ALMOST ANYONE WHO PUSHES THE BOUNDARIES GETS MY VOTE, MAYBE NOT A HIGH VOTE RE: THE CHALLENGE BUT AS AN ARTIST AND PHOTOGRAPHER.<br/>I GIVE IT A 1. LOVE YOUR WORK.</td>', 'I DONT SEE A LOT OF ROUND. I DONT FEEL ROUND. WILL SCORE POORLY FOR THOSE FACTS (DID IN FACT). HOWEVER I LIKE IT FOR ABSTRACTNESS. THE COLORS ARE COOL. ALMOST ANYONE WHO PUSHES THE BOUNDARIES GETS MY VOTE, MAYBE NOT A HIGH VOTE RE: THE CHALLENGE BUT AS AN ARTIST AND PHOTOGRAPHER.I GIVE IT A 1. LOVE YOUR WORK.', '2003-07-24 10:45:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(365929, 28865, 6458, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all the comments and votes!<br/> <br/>The border is a "flaw" in my teleconverter. This was actually shot with my polarizer (explaining the rich warm colours) and two UV filters on between my telelconverter and lens adapter. This was the only way I was able to get all of the vignetting circle into the frame. <br/> <br/>Would you belive that I completely didn''t think about the "literal representations of someone elses art" until about two days into the voting? It never even occured to me during the shooting, submission process.<br/> <br/>Rob: I think us Brighton based photographers are going to have to get together and come up with a shooting schedule. The piers seem to make their way into many challenges, and I know for a fact that the Beachyhead lighthouse was almost in the "From Above" challenge twice. <br/> <br/>Once again, thanks!<br/>-Matt</td>', 'Thanks for all the comments and votes! The border is a "flaw" in my teleconverter. This was actually shot with my polarizer (explaining the rich warm colours) and two UV filters on between my telelconverter and lens adapter. This was the only way I was able to get all of the vignetting circle into the frame.  Would you belive that I completely didn''t think about the "literal representations of someone elses art" until about two days into the voting? It never even occured to me during the shooting, submission process. Rob: I think us Brighton based photographers are going to have to get together and come up with a shooting schedule. The piers seem to make their way into many challenges, and I know for a fact that the Beachyhead lighthouse was almost in the "From Above" challenge twice.  Once again, thanks!-Matt', '2003-07-24 10:51:30.000000', NULL, 0),
(365931, 28709, 4493, '<td valign="top">This was taken at the Texas State Aquarium in Corpus Christi. They had a tank with several in it and they were lit by black light. I put my lens up to the glass and did a 1 second free hand pan on the jelly fish as it drifted in the water. I later did some contrast adjustments in PS to bring out the blue more.</td>', 'This was taken at the Texas State Aquarium in Corpus Christi. They had a tank with several in it and they were lit by black light. I put my lens up to the glass and did a 1 second free hand pan on the jelly fish as it drifted in the water. I later did some contrast adjustments in PS to bring out the blue more.', '2003-07-24 10:52:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(365933, 28865, 3087, '<td valign="top">:D</td>', ':D', '2003-07-24 10:52:48.000000', NULL, 0),
