(383399, 28264, 1647, '<td valign="top">I really like this shot.  It''s an interesting perspective on an object.  I would have considered perhaps three changes...  Possibly remove the small plant in front of the mushroom, possibly use some tin-foil or something similar to reflect a little more light under the mushroom, and possibly remove the out-of-focus object in the lower left corner.<br/> <br/>A lot of people are drawn to brighter objects and in this photo it is the top of the mushroom and the out-of-focus object in lower left.  Removing this object and lighting the underside of the mushroom slightly would have kept my focus on the mushroom more - it looks like there is a lot of detail and texture underneath to look at but it''s a little difficult.<br/> <br/>It''s still a great shot though.</td>', 'I really like this shot.  It''s an interesting perspective on an object.  I would have considered perhaps three changes...  Possibly remove the small plant in front of the mushroom, possibly use some tin-foil or something similar to reflect a little more light under the mushroom, and possibly remove the out-of-focus object in the lower left corner. A lot of people are drawn to brighter objects and in this photo it is the top of the mushroom and the out-of-focus object in lower left.  Removing this object and lighting the underside of the mushroom slightly would have kept my focus on the mushroom more - it looks like there is a lot of detail and texture underneath to look at but it''s a little difficult. It''s still a great shot though.', '2003-08-10 20:46:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(391140, 28393, 8860, '<td valign="top">That''s a great looking plant! Big, fat juicy lips too. Does it give off a rotting meat smell to attract the flies? <br/> <br/>Image is good but you''ve got a bit of noise going on - possibly due to oversharpening. It may be better to pull back a bit and leave the image slightly smaller but crisper. I think these plants have an interesting part at the top (which is cropped off) so I''d love to see this reshot, as the colours and lighting are really good. Did you use a tripod?</td>', 'That''s a great looking plant! Big, fat juicy lips too. Does it give off a rotting meat smell to attract the flies?  Image is good but you''ve got a bit of noise going on - possibly due to oversharpening. It may be better to pull back a bit and leave the image slightly smaller but crisper. I think these plants have an interesting part at the top (which is cropped off) so I''d love to see this reshot, as the colours and lighting are really good. Did you use a tripod?', '2003-08-18 04:08:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(399526, 28843, 9285, '<td valign="top">Great shot. I''m impressed with how you did it with a hand-held! Don''t know if you can mount an external flash. You might want to try bouncing the flash. It''ll create a softer effect and loss the shadow of the lollipop.<br/> <br/>Overall, it''s a beautiful shot. I like it.<br/></td>', 'Great shot. I''m impressed with how you did it with a hand-held! Don''t know if you can mount an external flash. You might want to try bouncing the flash. It''ll create a softer effect and loss the shadow of the lollipop. Overall, it''s a beautiful shot. I like it.', '2003-08-26 06:03:25.000000', NULL, 0),
